			"Message": "build(deps): bump @xterm/xterm from 6.1.0-beta.199 to 6.1.0-beta.202\n\nBumps [@xterm/xterm](https://github.com/xtermjs/xterm.js) from 6.1.0-beta.199 to 6.1.0-beta.202.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/xtermjs/xterm.js/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/xtermjs/xterm.js/commits)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: \"@xterm/xterm\"\n  dependency-version: 6.1.0-beta.202\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>",
			"SHA": "36a983a4a23d26141a13b6e1241e1fd98b3f1703"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T22:39:36Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				81,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Sky): Add missing SkyBridge initialization to Electron Layout\n\nThe Electron Layout was missing the SkyBridge step that already exists in Mountain.astro, causing the \"tree-views flash empty then pop\" flicker reported on the Electron profile.\n\nSkyBridge subscribes to Mountain's `cel:*` Tauri events (tree-view, SCM, debug, extensions) and fans them into the workbench consumers. Without it, every panel Mountain emits an event for paints empty on first frame and re-renders with data asynchronously.\n\nThis completes the Electron initialization chain: Preload → Polyfills → Bootstrap → Workbench → SkyBridge. The await chain ensures the workbench finishes its import before SkyBridge wires up consumers, so events pumped during boot reach listeners rather than firing into empty void.",
			"SHA": "0cf2e4da0a14818f7dd9c2e43465a484a1e26c75"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T21:18:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				81,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Sky): Remove hardcoded PostHog API key from source\n\nReplace the hardcoded PostHog API key with empty strings in both PostHogBridge.ts and astro.config.ts. The key should be sourced exclusively from the LAND_POSTHOG_KEY environment variable to prevent production credentials from being committed to the repository.\n\nThis sanitizes the codebase of the exposed `phc_...` key that was present in two locations.",
			"SHA": "9b67e2e6989c5a862bc1e6c4ee32b8e8f31a3fbd"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T17:24:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				81,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add tree-view data bridge for cel: events\n\nAdd a document listener for `cel:tree-view:create` that bridges tree view data between Mountain and the Sky frontend. When triggered, the listener invokes Mountain's `tree:getChildren` method and re-dispatches the returned items as `cel:tree-view:items` for any downstream renderer shim.\n\nThis completes the F1.1 handoff contract: Mountain emits `cel:tree-view:create` but nothing was listening, resulting in `consumer-present=false` in the cel-dispatch logs. The listener now primes the viewer by requesting root children and broadcasting them, eliminating the orphan event pattern.\n\nDev logging via `RenderDevLog` tracks both successful item retrieval (`bridge-items`) and failures (`bridge-error`) for debugging.\n\nAlso removes obsolete Step 13 comment from astro.config.ts regarding the built-in extension copy workaround.",
			"SHA": "4d9fb694ce1b313609c5c620583478aee4b09206"
		}
	],
